      "tags": " av002 fixture::new profile::baseline state::new ",
      "flds": "A box has three red blocks and two blue blocks. How many blocks are there in total?\u001fFive blocks.\u001fFive\u001fFive\n5\nThere are five blocks\u001fen-US\u001fThree plus two equals five.",
      "sfld": "A box has three red blocks and two blue blocks. How many blocks are there in total?",
      "csum": 3821054807,
      "flags": 0,
      "data": ""
    },
    {
      "id": 1789414083107,
      "guid": "k->?E#81OG",
      "mid": 1789414083101,
      "mod": 1789414083,
      "usn": -1,
      "tags": " av002 fixture::learning profile::baseline state::learning ",
      "flds": "Reverse the sequence red, blue, green.\u001fGreen, blue, red.\u001fGreen first\nBlue second\nRed last\u001fGreen blue red\u001fen-US\u001fReversing changes the order, not the items.",
      "sfld": "Reverse the sequence red, blue, green.",
      "csum": 3652334626,
      "flags": 0,
      "data": ""
    },
    {
      "id": 1789414083108,
      "guid": "BEV@KHI300",
      "mid": 1789414083101,
      "mod": 1789414083,
      "usn": -1,
      "tags": " av002 fixture::relearning profile::baseline state::relearning ",
      "flds": "In a game, a token is valid only if it is blue and square. A token is blue and round. Is it valid, and why?\u001fNo. It is blue but not square, and both conditions are required.\u001fIt is not valid\nIt fails the square requirement\u001fNo, because it is round instead of square.\u001fen-US\u001fMeeting just one required condition is insufficient.",
      "sfld": "In a game, a token is valid only if it is blue and square. A token is blue and round. Is it valid, and why?",
      "csum": 2170392721,
      "flags": 0,
      "data": ""
    },
    {
      "id": 1789414083109,
      "guid": "4;1`L.Ws+",
      "mid": 1789414083101,
      "mod": 1789414083,
      "usn": -1,
      "tags": " av002 fixture::mature profile::baseline state::mature ",
      "flds": "A machine sorts numbers from smallest to largest. Explain what it does to the list seven, two, five.\u001fIt returns two, five, seven, ordering the numbers from smallest to largest.\u001fThe resulting order is two, five, seven\u001fTwo five seven\u001fen-US\u001fThe values stay the same; only their order changes.",
      "sfld": "A machine sorts numbers from smallest to largest. Explain what it does to the list seven, two, five.",
      "csum": 3176705804,
